  "id": "context-mode",
  "title": "context-mode",
  "question": "How does context-mode keep bulky tool output out of an agent's context window while keeping it retrievable?",
  "summary": "Hooks steer calls that would flood the context to sandboxed ctx_* tools. Only printed output returns; large output is indexed in SQLite FTS5 and searched on demand.",
  "scope": "context-mode as wired for Claude Code: hook routing, the ctx_* MCP server with its subprocess sandbox and full-text store, and session-event capture.",
  "limits": [
    "Draws the Claude Code path of the 18 supported hosts; per-platform hooks, in-process adapters, the CLI, statistics and the web site are left out.",
    "Relations are calls and imports in the source, not runtime order; security internals and file handoffs between hooks and the server are not drawn."
  ],
